rockchip_ebc: printk-only DSP_END straggler instrumentation (quirk F)

DIAGNOSTIC-ONLY debug patch for the wilkbook quirk F investigation
(doc/driver-findings-report.md, finding 2026-07-12): detect the
straggler DSP_END credit that the zero-gap threshold-global analysis
predicts, directly in the kernel log, corruption visible or not.

Applied AFTER linux-pinenote-7.0-forward-port.patch, and ONLY by the
linux-pinenote-debug package variant (pinenote/packages/kernel.scm);
the primary linux-pinenote kernel remains byte-identical.  To remove,
delete this file and the linux-pinenote-debug variant.

No driver logic changes: every hunk either adds a printk/counter or
records which launch site set do_one_full_refresh.  Log lines:

  "ebc-dbg: straggler credit present at global launch (...)"
      completion_done(&ebc->display_end) was true immediately before
      the global's reinit_completion() -- an unconsumed DSP_END from
      the preceding activity existed at launch.

  "ebc-dbg: global wait returned R after E ms (...)"
      once per global refresh: wait_for_completion_timeout return
      value, elapsed ms, launch provenance (init/reset/resume/ioctl/
      threshold/offscreen), num_phases, nominal expected playback
      duration (~85 Hz frame clock), and the frame-timeout counters
      (last partial burst / total) so timeout-desync and extra-credit
      stragglers are distinguishable per event.

  "ebc-dbg: DSP_END irq with unconsumed credit" (rate-limited)
      a DSP_END arrived while the previous credit was still pending;
      completions are outrunning waits.

